/* progress.vh -- THE PER-LANE LIVENESS WATCHDOG, included by every bench.
 *
 * ⛔⛔⛔ WHY THIS FILE EXISTS, AND IT IS THE SHARPEST LESSON OF THE ARC. The
 * first self-clocked SHIFT build retired a clocked SHIFT after ONE dispatch
 * instead of sixteen, and ALL 75 SWEEP ARMS PASSED ON IT. Every bench's
 * success criterion was that pins MOVE -- `uio_oe` toggles, a trace is
 * non-empty -- and an action that retires early moves pins beautifully. The
 * defect was found by COVERAGE (the COLLECT phase's branch count was 0 in all
 * twelve benches), not by any bench.
 * ⇒ "The pins moved" is a VACUOUS success criterion. Progress is the real one,
 *   and nothing was asserting it.
 *
 * ⛔⛔ TWO LAYERS, AND THE SPLIT IS A RULING, NOT A STYLE CHOICE.
 *
 *   LAYER A -- universal liveness, COARSE, and deliberately independent of the
 *   golden model. Every lane's PC keeps advancing; no lane sits on one action
 *   past a generous bound; the writeback and retire counters are non-zero. It
 *   is crude on purpose, so it CANNOT be wrong in the same way the model could
 *   be: the model must not be its own only witness.
 *
 *   LAYER B -- exact per-action conformance. IT LIVES IN
 *   `test/clocked_conform.vh` AND SHIPS WITH THE CLOCKED RTL, not here,
 *   because its "is this a clocked action" predicate is `clk_real & level`
 *   -- which only MEANS self-clocked in the new engine. Landed earlier it
 *   would mis-fire on the pre-clocked corpus, and an `ifdef` nobody defines
 *   is a check that never runs, which is the very thing this file is about.
 *   It checks against `clocked_bounds.vh`,
 *   which is GENERATED by `model/clocked_phase.py` from measured runs. The
 *   model is the single authority for exact counts and NO BOUND IS RECOMPUTED
 *   HERE -- not even the SHIFT/SHIFTIN off-by-one (`OP_SHIFT` counts
 *   `a_cnt + 1` bits, `OP_SHIFTIN` counts `a_cnt`), because a constant written
 *   twice is this project's most expensive recurring defect.
 *
 * ⛔ WHAT IS DELIBERATELY EXEMPT, and why it is not a hole: a CHAINING
 * `OP_REARM` (op = REARM, level = 0) re-dispatches for ever BY DESIGN -- it is
 * ruling 2's mechanism for delays longer than the delay field, and it is how
 * every parked lane waits. A watchdog that failed on it would fire on every
 * bench in the suite, and the "fix" would be to delete the watchdog. So this
 * does NOT assert "every lane's PC always advances" unconditionally; it
 * asserts the thing that is actually always true.
 *
 * ⛔⛔ A TRAP THIS FILE FELL INTO AND MUST NOT AGAIN: the hook first read
 * `dut.u_eng.st === dut.u_eng.ST_WB`. A HIERARCHICAL REFERENCE TO A LOCALPARAM
 * compiled without complaint and the comparison was NEVER TRUE -- so the
 * watchdog ran on all twelve benches and checked nothing. A check that cannot
 * fire reads exactly like a check that passed. It is written as the literal
 * `2'd2`, with the encoding cited: `src/pe_engine.v` has
 * `localparam [1:0] ST_IDLE = 2'd0, ST_DRIVE = 2'd1, ST_WB = 2'd2`.
 * ⭐ The writeback counter in `pg_report` is what made that vacuity VISIBLE,
 * and it stays: "0 writebacks seen" must look different from "passed".
 *
 * ⛔⛔ AND A SECOND VACUITY TRAP IN THIS SAME FILE: every `$display` whose
 * format string was built by BRACE CONCATENATION -- `$display({"a %0d ",
 * "b %0d"}, x, y)` -- printed NOTHING AT ALL, while the counter beside it
 * incremented 144 times. A failure that counts itself and says nothing is
 * indistinguishable from a pass to anyone reading the log. ⇒ EVERY FORMAT
 * STRING HERE IS A SINGLE PLAIN LITERAL, however long the line.
 * ⭐ Both traps in this file had the same shape -- a check that cannot speak --
 * and both were caught only by comparing a COUNTER against the messages.
 *
 * ⭐ IT REPORTS BY PRINTING `*** FAIL`, which wires it into the existing machinery
 * for free: `test/coverage_sweep.sh` greps each arm's log for a case-sensitive
 * `FAIL`. And it self-reports in a `final` block, so no bench has to remember
 * to call anything -- a watchdog that only speaks when invited is silent in
 * exactly the bench nobody updated.
 *
 * USAGE:   `include "test/progress.vh"      // after the `dut` instance
 */

// ⭐ v2: the run-start anchor and the engine-started guard ride along, so
// every bench that has the watchdog has them too (test/runstart.vh)
`include "test/runstart.vh"

// ⛔ A DECLARED UPPER BOUND, not a second copy of N_LANES. The watchdog never
// iterates lanes -- it only touches the lane in `cur` -- so this sizes storage
// and nothing else. A lane index beyond it is REPORTED, not silently dropped.
localparam integer PG_MAXL  = 8;
// ⛔⛔ LAYER A's BOUND IS PER ACTION AND GENERATED (Wilson 11-14). It was a
// typed global 64 under a typed comment ("the longest is a 17-dispatch 8-bit
// clocked receive"); the USB buffer send holds ONE action for up to 112 wire
// bits, so five coverage arms read a false hang, and a stuck SHORT action (a
// self-timed SHIFTIN 8 bits late) stayed far under 64 and was invisible.
// ⇒ Each writeback is judged against the CURRENT action's own maximum,
//   `pe_isa.dispatch_max` emitted by test/gen_progress_bounds.py (that gate
//   holds this header fresh), picked from the engine's own decode below.
`include "test/progress_bounds.vh"
integer pg_bnd;                       // the current action's bound
reg [8*10:1] pg_kind;                 // ... and its kind, for the message

integer pg_n     [0:PG_MAXL-1];      // writebacks on the current action
integer pg_pc    [0:PG_MAXL-1];      // the PC they were at
integer pg_fa;
// ⛔⛔ A GLOBAL STALL DETECTOR WAS TRIED HERE AND REMOVED, because it
// CANNOT WORK and the reason is worth more than the check. Layer A counts
// dispatches ON an action, so it is blind to a lane that stops dispatching
// altogether -- which is what a lane parked for ever does, and it has cost
// two findings (a park with no fault bound hung the push-pull SPI master;
// M_BUS_NO_PULLDOWN survived every bench).
// ⚠ BUT A GLOBAL DETECTOR NEVER FIRES: MEASURED under
// M_BUS_NO_PULLDOWN, tb_trace still produced 1603 writebacks -- the other
// four lanes keep the engine busy -- while only 1 action retired against 110
// in the clean build. The engine was not stalled; ONE LANE was.
// ⛔ AND A PER-LANE VERSION CANNOT WORK EITHER: a lane parked on an OP_ARM
// edge legitimately never retires (UART-rx idling between frames), and from
// inside the bench nothing distinguishes that from a hang.
// ⇒ THAT AMBIGUITY IS WHAT THE DESIGN'S OWN FAULT BOUND IS FOR. A stuck bus
//   is detected by `CK_STRETCH_TO` in the engine, which HALTS the lane and
//   raises `clk_stretch_err`, and the bus-model mutant is priced against
//   THAT rather than against a bench heuristic. A check that cannot fire
//   would have been worse than no check: it reads as a pass.
integer pg_wbs, pg_acts;
integer pg_k;
reg     pg_oor;

initial begin
  for (pg_k = 0; pg_k < PG_MAXL; pg_k = pg_k + 1) begin
    pg_n[pg_k] = 0;  pg_pc[pg_k] = -1;
  end
  pg_fa = 0;
  pg_wbs = 0;  pg_acts = 0;
  pg_oor = 1'b0;
end

always @(posedge dut.clk) begin
  // the ENGINE's reset, not only the pin: a host RELOAD halts the engine through
  // its own reset (power-on OR halt) and the lane restarts at the SAME pc -- with
  // only `dut.rst_n` watched that restart counted as a second dispatch of one
  // action, which the per-action bound (11-14) read as a hang (run_reload tx1,
  // run_spitgt M3R; the old flat 64 had hidden it)
  if (dut.rst_n !== 1'b1 || dut.u_eng.rst_n !== 1'b1) begin
    for (pg_k = 0; pg_k < PG_MAXL; pg_k = pg_k + 1) begin
      pg_n[pg_k] = 0;  pg_pc[pg_k] = -1;
    end
  end else if (dut.u_eng.st === 2'd2) begin
       // ST_WB -- literal, see above
    pg_wbs = pg_wbs + 1;
    if (dut.u_eng.cur >= PG_MAXL) begin
      if (!pg_oor) begin
        pg_oor = 1'b1;
        $display("*** FAIL progress.vh: lane index %0d exceeds PG_MAXL=%0d -- the watchdog cannot see every lane; raise PG_MAXL rather than trust a partial check", dut.u_eng.cur, PG_MAXL);
        pg_fa = pg_fa + 1;
      end
    end else if (dut.u_eng.a_op === 3'd7 && dut.u_eng.a_lvl === 1'b0) begin
      pg_n[dut.u_eng.cur]  = 0;                   // the chaining re-arm
      pg_pc[dut.u_eng.cur] = dut.u_eng.l_pc[dut.u_eng.cur];
    end else begin
      if (pg_pc[dut.u_eng.cur] !== dut.u_eng.l_pc[dut.u_eng.cur]) begin
        // the PC moved: the previous action at this lane has RETIRED
        if (pg_pc[dut.u_eng.cur] !== -1) pg_acts = pg_acts + 1;
        pg_pc[dut.u_eng.cur]  = dut.u_eng.l_pc[dut.u_eng.cur];
        pg_n[dut.u_eng.cur]   = 1;
      end else begin
        pg_n[dut.u_eng.cur] = pg_n[dut.u_eng.cur] + 1;
      end
      // ---- LAYER A: per-action liveness, model-independent ----------------
      // The kind is read off the engine's OWN decode of the current action
      // (wires, never localparams -- see the ST_WB trap above): the hold rule
      // `ck_hold = (ck_act & ~ck_retire) | (st_act & ~(st_last & ~usb_stuff))`.
`ifdef PE_V1_RTL
      // v1-lock's engine (gate_v2_equiv's v1 side) has no self-timed / USB
      // decode to read: the ruling's FALLBACK, the generated global maximum
      // over every legitimate action (the USB send is the largest kind)
      pg_bnd = PG_USB_SEND_MAX;                            pg_kind = "v1-global";
      if (1'b0) begin
`else
      if (dut.u_eng.usb_send === 1'b1) begin
        pg_bnd = PG_USB_SEND_MAX;                          pg_kind = "usb_send";
`endif
      end else if (dut.u_eng.ck_shift === 1'b1) begin
        pg_bnd = pg_max_ck_shift(dut.u_eng.a_cnt);         pg_kind = "ck_shift";
      end else if (dut.u_eng.ck_shiftin === 1'b1) begin
        pg_bnd = pg_max_ck_shiftin(dut.u_eng.a_cnt);       pg_kind = "ck_shiftin";
`ifndef PE_V1_RTL
      end else if (dut.u_eng.usb_act === 1'b1) begin
        pg_bnd = pg_max_usb_rx(dut.u_eng.a_cnt);           pg_kind = "usb_rx";
      end else if (dut.u_eng.st_act === 1'b1) begin
        // cur_cls[1] is C_SHIFT (a literal: see the ST_WB trap)
        if (dut.u_eng.cur_cls[1] === 1'b1) begin
          pg_bnd = pg_max_st_shift(dut.u_eng.a_cnt);       pg_kind = "st_shift";
        end else begin
          pg_bnd = pg_max_st_shiftin(dut.u_eng.a_cnt);     pg_kind = "st_shiftin";
        end
`endif
      end else begin
`ifndef PE_V1_RTL
        pg_bnd = PG_OTHER_MAX;                             pg_kind = "other";
`endif
      end
      if (pg_n[dut.u_eng.cur] == pg_bnd + 1) begin
        $display("*** FAIL progress.vh[A]: lane %0d has sat on the action at pc=%0d for %0d dispatches (its own bound %0d, kind %0s) -- it is NOT RETIRING", dut.u_eng.cur, pg_pc[dut.u_eng.cur], pg_n[dut.u_eng.cur], pg_bnd, pg_kind);
        pg_fa = pg_fa + 1;
      end
    end
  end
end

// ⛔⛔⛔ THE LOAD-MODE INTERLOCK, AND IT HAS MISLED FOUR TIMES. In LOAD
// mode `ui_in[5]` is PIN_PTR, not the host queue tag -- so a host PUSH
// issued while PROG is high RESETS THE LOAD POINTER instead of pushing. It
// is silent: the image is quietly corrupted and the symptom surfaces much
// later as nonsense the engine executes.
// ⚠ MEASURED, in `tb_fifo`'s first version: 81 of 87 store bytes differed
// from the image, and what it LOOKED like was an RTL defect -- Layer B
// reporting 24 clocked actions disagreeing with the model on `op=2 cnt=0`,
// an action the image does not contain.
// ⛔⛔ IT CANNOT BE GUARDED AT THE PINS, and the first version of this guard
// tried: a WR strobe with PROG high is EXACTLY WHAT THE LOADER DOES, so
// watching the pins fires on every bench's own load. The pins are
// multiplexed -- that IS the hazard -- so nothing at the pin level
// distinguishes a load write from a stray push.
// ⇒ THE GUARD IS ON THE BENCH'S INTENT. A bench raises `pg_pushing` while it
//   means to drive the HOST CHANNEL -- `host_feed.vh` drives it from `hf_en`,
//   and a bench that pushes by hand sets it around its own strobes -- and
//   pushing while PROG is high is then a declared contradiction rather than
//   an indistinguishable waveform.
// ⚠ A bench deliberately testing load-mode behaviour sets `pg_loadmode_ok`.
// ⛔⛔ EXPECTED QUIESCENCE, DECLARED BY THE BENCH THAT KNOWS IT. The
// anti-vacuity check above ("no action was observed to retire") is right for
// an ordinary arm and WRONG for a REFUSAL arm, where the whole claim is that
// the engine does NOT proceed: a 1.6x alias halts the lane, a cfgerr refusal
// never dispatches, an ARM on a reserved pin can never fire. ⚠ MEASURED: the
// moment the sweep could finally SEE these verdicts, exactly four arms went
// red -- tb_pinrange refuse and armnone, tb_status overrun, tb_tx badclk --
// and every one of them is a refusal test.
// ⇒ So the bench DECLARES it, per ARM rather than per bench (tb_tx's `clean`
//   arm must still be checked while `badclk` must not), and the declaration
//   is a claim the bench makes about itself rather than a silent exemption.
reg pg_quiescent_ok = 1'b0;  // this arm EXPECTS no action to retire
reg pg_pushing    = 1'b0;   // the bench intends to drive the host channel
reg pg_loadmode_ok = 1'b0;  // ... and means to do it in LOAD mode
integer pg_badpush;
initial pg_badpush = 0;
always @(posedge dut.clk) if (dut.rst_n === 1'b1) begin
  if (pg_pushing && !pg_loadmode_ok && dut.ui_in[7] === 1'b1) begin
    if (pg_badpush == 0) begin
      $display("*** FAIL progress.vh[A]: the bench drove the HOST CHANNEL while PROG=1 -- in load mode ui_in[5] is PIN_PTR, so a push RESETS THE LOAD POINTER and corrupts the image silently (set pg_loadmode_ok if that is the test)");
      pg_fa = pg_fa + 1;
    end
    pg_badpush = pg_badpush + 1;
  end
end

// ---- LAYER S: NO LANE WAITS FOR ANOTHER LANE'S WORD ((b'), Wilson 11-14) ----
// ⛔⛔ THE DISPATCHER USED TO STALL EVERY LANE when the EDF winner's head was
// empty (agent 2, 729111f): a word arriving late after a branch held up the
// USB lane's samples too. (b') picks only lanes whose head is valid, so while
// the schedule runs, an idle engine with no armed winner and SOME released
// lane holding a valid head MUST dispatch that cycle. A cycle where it does
// not is the global stall back -- `M_GLOBAL_STALL` is this layer's must-fire.
integer pg_sblk;
initial pg_sblk = 0;
// ⚠ `PE_EQUIV_PRE` is set ONLY by test/gate_batch_equiv.py's PRE-batch build:
// that RTL has no `rdy_rel` (the old `ready` IS the released term) and no (b'),
// so this layer does not apply to it. It never drives a pin.
`ifndef PE_EQUIV_PRE
always @(posedge dut.clk) if (dut.rst_n === 1'b1) begin
  if (dut.u_eng.now_inc === 1'b1 && dut.u_eng.st === 2'd0 && dut.u_eng.config_err !== 1'b1
      && dut.u_eng.w_armed !== 1'b1 && (|(dut.u_eng.rdy_rel & dut.u_eng.hv))
      && dut.u_eng.cur_ld !== 1'b1) begin
    if (pg_sblk == 0) begin
      $display("*** FAIL progress.vh[S]: a released lane with a VALID head waited while the engine idled -- another lane's empty head is holding the dispatcher (the global stall (b') removed)");
      pg_fa = pg_fa + 1;
    end
    pg_sblk = pg_sblk + 1;
  end
end
`endif

// ⛔⛔ THE REPORT IS THE `final` BLOCK ITSELF, NOT A TASK IT CALLS.
// It was `task pg_report` invoked from `final`, which Verilator accepts and
// iverilog refuses ("final procedures cannot enable/call tasks").
// That one line kept `test/gate_corpus_trace.py` -- the TWO-SIMULATOR
// corpus comparison -- from building since `7a672b0`, and because that
// gate was in no list, nothing noticed (ruling Q2). The task had exactly
// one caller, so folding it in changes nothing Verilator does.
final begin
    // ⛔ DID-NOT-RUN MUST NOT LOOK LIKE PASSED. These two counters exist
    // because this file was once vacuous on every bench and said nothing.
    $display("  progress.vh[A]: %0d writeback(s), %0d action(s) retired",
             pg_wbs, pg_acts);
    if (pg_quiescent_ok && pg_acts == 0)
      $display("  progress.vh[A]: quiescent BY DECLARATION -- this arm expects no action to retire (a refusal test)");
    else if (pg_wbs == 0)
      $display("*** FAIL progress.vh: no writeback was ever observed, so the liveness check had nothing to check");
    else if (pg_acts == 0)
      $display("*** FAIL progress.vh: no action was observed to retire, so the liveness check had nothing to check");
    else if (pg_fa == 0)
      $display("  progress.vh[A]: ok -- per-action liveness clean");
    else
      $display("*** FAIL progress.vh[A]: %0d liveness failure(s)", pg_fa);
  end

